5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.044113488029123626,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":57.6,"_gate_rev_durability":0.11633409531278249,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":83.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.023566295165892284,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":37.3,"_gate_share_shrink":0.005702914063247855,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":42.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.01171296792877829,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":80.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.21248,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.8,"_gp_insider_buying":true,"_score_insider_buying":80.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Fidelity D & D Bancorp, Inc. operates as the bank holding company for The Fidelity Deposit and Discount Bank that provides a range of banking, trust, and financial services to individuals, small businesses, and corporate customers. The company accepts savings, club, interest-bearing and non-interest-bearing checking, money market, and short- and long-term time deposits, as well as certificates of deposit. It also offers commercial and industrial, commercial real estate, consumer, and residential mortgage loans. In addition, the company provides government and healthcare banking services, cash management and merchant services, and credit and debit cards; and alternative financial and insurance products with asset management services, as well as online banking, telephone banking, and digital wallet. The company was founded in 1902 and is headquartered in Dunmore, Pennsylvania.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Daniel J. Santaniello | President, CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 298 people. Revenue per employee of $313K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 79%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $83K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Fidelity D & D Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $399M market cap on $93M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +2% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 14-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $25M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 27 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.50\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insiders hold 21% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2980189491817422},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 10% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Trading at a 55% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Insiders are net buyers (80% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","25 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Liquidity Mapping Around (FDBC) Price Events","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/89/Liquidity_Mapping_Around_FDBC_Price_Events_110126043002_1793525402.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793525402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Daniel J. Santaniello Gifts 200 Shares of Fidelity D & D Bancorp Inc (FDBC) on October 27, 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/daniel-j-santaniello-gifts-200-shares-of-fidelity-d-d-bancorp-inc-fdbc-on-october-27-2026","date":"2026-10-28","timestamp":1793207200.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Fidelity D D Bancorp (NASDAQ: FDBC) lifts quarterly profit 21% on higher income","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/24/fidelity-d-d-bancorp-nasdaq-fdbc-lifts-quarterly-profit-21-on-higher-income.html","date":"2026-10-24","timestamp":1792868582.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.612,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Fidelity D&D Bancorp Inc. (NASDAQ:FDBC) Announces Dividend Increase \u2013 $0.46 Per Share","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/23/fidelity-dd-bancorp-inc-nasdaqfdbc-announces-dividend-increase-0-46-per-share.html","date":"2026-10-23","timestamp":1792761082.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.84,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"Fidelity D&D Bancorp raises quarterly dividend by 7% to $0.46/share (NASDAQ:FDBC)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4656118-fidelity-dd-bancorp-raises-quarterly-dividend-by-7-to-046share","date":"2026-10-22","timestamp":1792693130.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.34,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance","dividend"]},{"title":"Fidelity D And D Bancorp (FDBC) Q3 Earni